// stdlib/pbpk/mod.sio - Public exports for the pbpk module (CONVENTIONS §2).
//
// This file is the re-export surface mandated by stdlib/CONVENTIONS.md §2.
// It declares only `pub use` lines; no implementations live here. All
// rapamycin PBPK, covariate, error model, regulatory, stent-release,
// population, and validation code is defined in the sibling `.sio` files
// and re-exposed through this module.
//
// The pbpk module provides physiologically-based pharmacokinetic
// modeling primitives for clinical rapamycin modeling: 2-compartment
// and 3-compartment ODE integrators, dose-response / AUC / trough
// gates, covariate and error models, population PK, regulatory and
// clinical validators, and stent drug-release simulations.
//
// Coexistence with lib.sio: this file is the re-export surface; the
// sibling `lib.sio` is the module-identity marker (`module pbpk`).
// Both files coexist; `lib.sio` is not modified by this contract.

